{"author":{"id":"85a3c31a64931f83958f26b24045fef8415ea6ff04d942d15661891c77fc0695"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1794213118,"nonce":"5PN23r4NzuWyx90X/fGWuqeaUE8=","message":"Added (working tree): texture methods and WGSL-named free functions, typed by the texture's dimension and kind: sample (implicit level, fragment only), sample_level (float level, or integer for depth), load (integer coords and level, or sample index when multisampled; cube rejected), dimensions (u32, UVec2 or UVec3). Integer textures are loaded, not sampled. Derivatives dpdx, dpdy, fwidth (method or function). discard!() as a statement or a branch tail; it counts as leaving the function for return-path checks. A vertex or compute entry point that reaches a derivative, discard!() or implicit-level sample is an error at that operation, naming the entry point.\n\nAlso: MSL is written for version 2.1 (naga's default 1.0 rejects instance_id); a module needing what GLSL ES 3.00 lacks (storage buffers) gets no GLSL, with Artifacts::glsl_missing saying why, instead of failing the compile; the ariadne renderer now indexes by byte, since non-ASCII text above an error shifted its label.\n\nStill open here: f16 literals, array lengths from constants, swizzle assignment, uniform layout rules, trybuild span tests.","files":null}]}